-- Refresh only the original bundled English markup help article.
-- Preserve customized/localized help, permissions, revisions and unrelated articles.
UPDATE `aowow_articles`
SET `article` = '[menu tab=2 path=2,13,7]Use markup to format comments and guides and link to local database entries. The editor toolbar inserts common tags. This reference also covers grid tables, map pins, dungeon floors and tabbed guide sections. Maps and tabs require staff-level author permissions; ordinary comments cannot enable those features.\n\n[h2]Formatting Tags[/h2]\n[h3]Bold[/h3]\n\\[b]text[/b]\n\n[h3]Line break[/h3]\n\\[br] -> inserts a line break.\n\n[h3]Code[/h3]\n\\[code]text[/code] -> creates a block of text that ignores markup and uses a monospace font.\n\n[h3]Horizontal Rule[/h3]\n\\[hr] -> creates a horizontal rule\n\n[h3]Italics[/h3]\n\\[i]text[/i] -> [i]text[/i]\n\n[h3]Preformatted text[/h3]\n\\[pre]text[/pre] -> shows text with all whitespace preserved in a monospace font, but allows markup\n\n[h3]Strikethrough[/h3]\n\\[s]text[/s] -> [s]text[/s]\n\n[h3]Small text[/h3]\n\\[small]text[/small] -> [small]text[/small]\n\n[h3]Subscript[/h3]\n\\[sub]text[/sub] -> [sub]text[/sub]\n\n[h3]Superscript[/h3]\n\\[sup]text[/sup] -> [sup]text[/sup]\n\n[h3]Underline[/h3]\n\\[u]text[/u] -> [u]text[/u]\n\n[h2]Database Tags[/h2]\n\n\nDatabase tags use the record ID from the local database page and fill in its name automatically. Leave site/domain unset to keep normal database links local.\n\n[h3]Achievements[/h3]\n\\[achievement=3579] -> [achievement=3579]\n\n[h3]Classes[/h3]\n\\[class=11] -> [class=11]\n\n[h3]Events[/h3]\n\\[event=1] -> [event=1]\n\nUse the game-event ID shown in the event page URL, not the client holiday ID. For example, the default Lunar Festival event is 7; 327 is its holiday ID. Imported event IDs can differ between installations. For a named local link, use an explicit query-string prefix:\n[code]\\[url=?event=7]Lunar Festival\\[/url][/code]\n\n[h3]Factions[/h3]\n\\[faction=749] -> [faction=749]\n\n[h3]Items[/h3]\n\\[item=12345] -> [item=12345]\n\nTo hide the icon: \\[item=12345 icon=false] -> [item=12345 icon=false]\n\n[h3]Itemsets[/h3]\n\\[itemset=699] -> [itemset=699]\n\n[h3]NPCs[/h3]\n\\[npc=32906] -> [npc=32906]\n\n[h3]Objects[/h3]\n\\[object=1733] -> [object=1733]\n\n[h3]Pets[/h3]\n\\[pet=45] -> [pet=45]\n\n[h3]Quests[/h3]\n\\[quest=7981] -> [quest=7981]\n\n[h3]Races[/h3]\n\\[race=11] -> [race=11]\n\n[b]To specify the gender of the icon:[/b] \\[race=11 gender=1] -> [race=11 gender=1] - 0 is male, 1 is female\n\n[h3]Skills[/h3]\n\\[skill=171] -> [skill=171]\n\n[h3]Spells[/h3]\n\\[spell=52398] -> [spell=52398]\n\\[spell=31565 buff=true] -> [spell=31565 buff=true]\n\n[h3]Statistics[/h3]\n\\[statistic=1076] -> [statistic=1076]\n\n[h3]Zones[/h3]\n\\[zone=3959] -> [zone=3959]\n\n[h2]HTML Tags[/h2]\n\n[h3]Anchor[/h3]\n\\[anchor=text] -> creates an anchor with the name "text" at this point.\n\n[h3]Ordered List[/h3]\n\\[ol]\\[li]list item[/li][/ol] -> [ol][li]list item[/li][/ol]\n\n[h3]Tables[/h3]\n[b]\\[table][/b]\nBorder: \\[table border=2]\nSpacing: \\[table cellspacing=2]\nPadding: \\[table cellpadding=2]\nWidth: \\[table width=500px] - Valid units are px, em, %\n\n[b]\\[tr][/b] - No attributes\n\n[b]\\[td][/b]\nAlign: \\[td align=right] - Valid options are left, right, center, justify\nVertical align: \\[td valign=baseline] - Valid options are top, middle, bottom, baseline\nColumn span: \\[td colspan=2]\nRow span: \\[td rowspan=2]\nWidth: \\[td width=500px] - Valid units are px, em, %\n\n[h3]Grid tables and header cells[/h3]\nUse \\[table class=grid] for a styled guide table and \\[td=header] for column headers. Put each row inside \\[tr] and each cell inside \\[td] or \\[td=header]. Prefer a compact table describing what to do, when to do it and where to go.\n\n[code]\\[table class=grid]\n\\[tr]\\[td=header]What\\[/td]\\[td=header]When\\[/td]\\[td=header]Where\\[/td]\\[/tr]\n\\[tr]\\[td]NPC or boss\\[/td]\\[td]Required quest stage or encounter\\[/td]\\[td]Zone, floor and coordinates\\[/td]\\[/tr]\n\\[/table][/code]\n\n[table class=grid]\n[tr][td=header]What[/td][td=header]When[/td][td=header]Where[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]NPC or boss[/td][td]Required quest stage or encounter[/td][td]Zone, floor and coordinates[/td][/tr]\n[/table]\n\nGrid styling and header cells are present in the initial HTML, including when JavaScript is disabled. Wide tables scroll within their own area on small screens. Avoid fixed pixel widths unless they are necessary.\n\n[h3]Unordered List[/h3]\n\\[ul]\\[li]list item[/li][/ul] -> [ul][li]list item[/li][/ul]\n\n[h2]Guide Maps and Tabs[/h2]\n[b]These tags require staff-level author permissions.[/b] They are intended for guide and article content.\n\n[h3]Maps and linked pins[/h3]\nUse \\[map zone=ID] with one or more \\[pin] tags. Each pin needs x and y coordinates and a readable label; url is optional and can link to an NPC, boss, quest or another local database page.\n\n[code]\\[map zone=4812 floor=5]\n\\[pin x=8.9 y=53.8 url=?npc=36678]Professor Putricide\\[/pin]\n\\[/map][/code]\n\n[b]Example output[/b]\n[map zone=4812 floor=5]\n[pin x=8.9 y=53.8 url=?npc=36678]Professor Putricide[/pin]\n[/map]\n\n[ul][li]zone is the local zone ID, not a continent or world-coordinate identifier.[/li][li]For an outdoor map, omit floor. For a dungeon, floor is the client floor number, not the position in a list. In this example, floor 5 selects The Upper Reaches in Icecrown Citadel.[/li][li]x and y are percentages on that exact map image: use values from 0 to below 100, with at most one decimal place. Do not paste world coordinates or coordinates from another floor.[/li][li]Use an explicit local query link such as ?npc=36678 or ?quest=7981 for the pin destination.[/li][li]Interactive maps require JavaScript and the corresponding generated map images and zone data. Without JavaScript, pin labels, safe links and coordinates remain readable.[/li][/ul]\n\n[h3]Separate locations into tabs[/h3]\nUse a unique tabs name and place each location inside its own tab. Quote tab names that contain spaces. Keep a guide to three visible maps; use separate tabs if it needs more.\n\n[code]\\[tabs name=guide-locations]\n\\[tab name="The Upper Reaches"]\n\\[map zone=4812 floor=5]\n\\[pin x=8.9 y=53.8 url=?npc=36678]Professor Putricide\\[/pin]\n\\[/map]\n\\[/tab]\n\\[tab name="Encounter details"]\n\\[npc=36678] is in \\[zone=4812].\n\\[ul]\n\\[li]Floor: The Upper Reaches (client floor 5).\\[/li]\n\\[li]Map pin: 8.9, 53.8.\\[/li]\n\\[/ul]\n\\[/tab]\n\\[/tabs][/code]\n\n[b]Example output[/b]\n[tabs name=guide-locations]\n[tab name="The Upper Reaches"]\n[map zone=4812 floor=5]\n[pin x=8.9 y=53.8 url=?npc=36678]Professor Putricide[/pin]\n[/map]\n[/tab]\n[tab name="Encounter details"]\n[npc=36678] is in [zone=4812].\n[ul]\n[li]Floor: The Upper Reaches (client floor 5).[/li]\n[li]Map pin: 8.9, 53.8.[/li]\n[/ul]\n[/tab]\n[/tabs]\n\nTab switching requires JavaScript. Keep essential directions and pin labels meaningful as text so the initial HTML is useful too.\n\n[h2]URLs[/h2]\n\\[url=https://www.google.com]Google[/url] -> [url=https://www.google.com]Google[/url]\n\\[url]https://www.google.com[/url] -> [url]https://www.google.com[/url]\n\\[url=http://www.google.com rel=item=12345]Rel link[/url] -> [url=http://www.google.com rel=item=12345]Rel link[/url]\nThe rel attribute adds an item tooltip while the link still opens Google.\n\nFor local database links, keep the question mark:\n[code]\\[url=?quest=7981]Quest details\\[/url][/code]'
WHERE `url` = 'help=markup-guide' AND `locale` = 0 AND `rev` = 0 AND `editAccess` = 2
    AND `type` IS NULL AND `typeId` IS NULL
    AND SHA2(`article`, 256) IN ('1e42f4953ff4c46c8c354d70bde2d1730019ecf898c535247f93a83ada4ea648');

-- Replace only the obsolete Import paragraph; retain surrounding editorial text.
UPDATE `aowow_articles`
SET `article` = REPLACE(`article`, '[li][b]Import[/b] – Displays a pop-up text window where you can enter the URL of a talent build made with [url=http://www.wowarmory.com/talent-calc.xml]Blizzard\'s talent calculator[/url]. Be sure that you first select the "Link to this build" option in the Blizzard talent calculator so that the URL will be properly formatted for importing.[/li]', '[li][b]Import[/b] – Opens a prompt for a saved Wrath-era talent-build URL. It accepts legacy formats such as ?cid=CLASS_ID&tal=RANK_DIGITS, or a class-name URL containing ?tal=RANK_DIGITS. The build is parsed locally; no external calculator is needed. To load a build shared by this site\'s calculator, open its ?talent#... link directly.[/li]')
WHERE `url` = 'help=talent-calculator' AND `locale` = 0 AND `rev` = 0 AND `editAccess` = 2
    AND `type` IS NULL AND `typeId` IS NULL;

-- Remove obsolete local forum destinations and refresh stat-help contact/credit links.
UPDATE `aowow_articles`
SET `article` = REPLACE(`article`, ', or post on our [url=/?forums&board=1]forums[/url]', '')
WHERE `url` IN ('help=item-comparison','help=profiler','help=stat-weighting','help=talent-calculator') AND `locale` IN (0)
    AND `rev` = 0 AND `editAccess` = 2 AND `type` IS NULL AND `typeId` IS NULL;

